---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Cloudways vs DigitalOcean: Managed vs Unmanaged - VPSTier.com">
  <section class="hero-gradient border-b border-white/5">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
      <a href="/blog" class="text-orange-500 hover:text-orange-400 text-sm mb-6 block">← Back to Blog</a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="badge badge-blue">Comparison</span>
        <span class="text-gray-500 text-sm">May 20, 2025</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Cloudways vs DigitalOcean: Managed vs Unmanaged for Beginners</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 text-lg mb-6">Cloudways offers managed cloud hosting while DigitalOcean gives you raw infrastructure. Which is better for developers just starting with VPS?</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Cloudways</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">DigitalOcean</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Managed Hosting</span>
        <span class="text-xs text-gray-400 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-white/10">Beginners</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <article class="prose prose-invert prose-orange max-w-none">
      <h2>The Fundamental Difference</h2>
      <p><strong>DigitalOcean</strong> = You get a VM and figure everything out yourself. SSH access, nginx config, SSL certificates, cron jobs — all on you.</p>
      <p><strong>Cloudways</strong> = They manage the server, you focus on your app. One-click LAMP/LEMP stack, automatic backups, built-in SSH/SFTP.</p>

      <h2>When to Choose Each</h2>
      <p>Choose <strong>DigitalOcean</strong> if:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You know your way around Linux</li>
        <li>You want maximum control and lowest cost</li>
        <li>You're comfortable debugging server issues</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Choose <strong>Cloudways</strong> if:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>You want to deploy fast without DevOps knowledge</li>
        <li>You're running client sites and need managed backups</li>
        <li>You prefer predictable pricing with no surprise infra bills</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Commission Comparison</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudways</strong>: $50-175 per sale (one of the highest in hosting)</li>
        <li><strong>DigitalOcean</strong>: $25 credit per referred user</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Cloudways pays significantly better for affiliates.</p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
